	quest.0F426527B63F854D.title: "Simply Swords"
	quest.0F55EC9DC495A7A2.quest_desc: [
		"&3Recipes &rneed to be encoded into &bpatterns&r to be usable by crafting &bCPUs&r."
		"{image:fzzy_config:textures/gui/sprites/widget/popup/divider.png width:200 height:15 align:center}"
		"The encoded &bpatterns&r need to be put into &6Pattern Providers&r on the same network as the &dCrafting CPU&r itself."
		"{image:fzzy_config:textures/gui/sprites/widget/popup/divider.png width:200 height:15 align:center}"
		"When the &dCrafting CPU&r then needs to craft the primary result of that pattern, it'll delegate this to the pattern provider."
		"{image:fzzy_config:textures/gui/sprites/widget/popup/divider.png width:200 height:15 align:center}"
		"Normally, the &dPattern Provider&r will then push out the ingredients to an adjacent block (a &aMolecular Assembler&r for crafting recipes, for example), and crafting continues once the result enters the network again."
		""
		"{@pagebreak}"
		"This can be achieved by pushing the crafting result back into the pattern provider, an &9ME Interface&r or any other means that would import the crafting result into the network."
		"{image:fzzy_config:textures/gui/sprites/widget/popup/divider.png width:200 height:15 align:center}"
		"&aMolecular Assemblers&r are smart enough to automatically return the crafting result to the same pattern provider that provided the ingredients."
	]
